
# config

## errors
- label: When the config YAML is invalid (bad syntax, duplicate panel names, reference to unknown source, etc.), the process prints a clear error starting with 'config:' and exits without starting the server
  command: PACE_CONFIG=/nonexistent/path/config.yaml bun run src/cli.ts 2>&1 | head -1 | grep -q 'config: file not found'

## presets
- Users can start with a ready-made configuration using --preset tech-news (or ml-ai, academic-papers, product-launches, etc.) instead of writing their own config.yaml

# adapters

## contract
- When a source fails to fetch (network error, bad response, parse error), the log and error message clearly identify which source had the problem
- mastodon, lobsters, youtube, podcast, stackexchange, and github adapters previously swallowed fetch errors (non-2xx, network, parse) via console.warn + return [] or null; after minimal fixes they now throw Error messages starting with '<name>: ' (e.g. 'mastodon: failed to fetch...') per the Adapter contract documented in src/adapters/types.ts and oz1 @spec @implemented
- 16 of 17 adapters' fetch methods comply with the contract in types.ts: throw on network/!2xx/parse/auth errors with name: prefix using errorMessage helper (twitter intentionally returns []+log without attempting fetch per its ox1 design; explicit no-sources [] only in configured cases for others) @spec @implemented
- The .facts file, relevant adapter source, and their .test.ts were updated (minimal diffs) so that contract-violating swallow behaviors are removed and tests assert the throwing behavior instead; no unrelated changes, no new features (e.g. no reddit OAuth) @spec @implemented

## reddit
- reddit adapter fetch for any public subreddit always fails with 403 (message starts with 'reddit: failed to fetch ...: 403' or wrapped); confirmed even using browser User-Agent + Accept headers on both www.reddit.com and old.reddit.com (upstream blocking of unauthenticated .json API access; not fixable with headers/UA; requires OAuth app + credentials or authenticated session) @spec @implemented
- config.example.yaml documents reddit as commented example (with note that it requires credentials due to upstream 403; no functional change to yaml; other presets untouched per smallest-change scope) @spec @implemented

## out-of-box
- Of the 17 adapters, the following work out-of-the-box returning real public content with no credentials/secrets (using only basic params from config.example or defaults): hackernews, lobsters, devto, arxiv, rss, wikipedia, stackexchange, npm (keywords), lemmy, producthunt, podcast (public feeds), youtube (public channels), github (trending mode and releases atom mode), mastodon (with hashtags or accounts), github-releases (anon in some envs; caveats per nzg) @spec @implemented
- Live one-by-one re-tests (bun -e imports + fetch with configs from *.test.ts and config.*.yaml) confirm: reddit and twitter cannot work out-of-the-box without credentials; the other 15 (incl. github-releases with anon caveats per nzg) can (with caveats for mastodon some endpoints); reddit root cause is upstream 403 on public .json not solvable without auth @spec @implemented

## twitter
- twitter adapter never returns real Items out-of-the-box; it always logs a message about requiring credentials and returns [] (even if lists/searches configured); this is by design as it has no unauthenticated public fetch path @spec @implemented

## github-releases
- github-releases adapter (the dedicated API one) can return real release Items with anon unauth request in some environments (e.g. low rate), but may receive 403 or rate limit errors on api.github.com without token param; its error path correctly throws 'github-releases: ' per contract (unlike some other adapters) @spec @implemented

## status
- hackernews adapter works out-of-the-box: public unauth fetch to firebaseio.com returns real Items (verified via bun -e with default params) @spec @implemented
- lobsters adapter works out-of-the-box with public unauth JSON (verified); its internal fetch now throws on !ok per contract (test updated) @spec @implemented
- mastodon adapter can work out-of-the-box for hashtags/accounts on public instances (verified bun -e); public timeline may 422 but now correctly throws 'mastodon: ' error instead of swallowing (contract fix + test update) @spec @implemented
- youtube, podcast, stackexchange adapters work out-of-the-box on public endpoints (verified); now throw on fetch errors with prefix instead of warn+[] (contract + tests updated) @spec @implemented
- github adapter (trending + atom releases) works out-of-the-box (public scrape/Atom verified); its error paths updated to throw per contract (smallest change in fetchGithubResource and callers) @spec @implemented
- devto, arxiv, rss, wikipedia, npm, lemmy, producthunt adapters work out-of-the-box with public unauth fetches (verified via live bun -e one-by-one re-tests using example configs) @spec @implemented

## quality
- stackexchange adapter source contains no dead/unused 'warnAndReturnEmpty' helper function (nor its multi-line comment claiming to centralize warn+return[] for fetch errors); the dead code was removed after its call sites in !ok/catch were updated to throw per the Adapter contract and errorMessage usage in types.ts (verifiable by: ! grep -q 'warnAndReturnEmpty' src/adapters/stackexchange.ts ) @implemented
- podcast adapter source contains no over-engineered 'warnAndReturnEmpty' helper function (nor its multi-line JSDoc claiming to 'Centralize the repeated warn + return [] pattern used for recoverable fetch/parse issues'); after prior contract updates the helper is only called from one site and has been inlined there for simplicity (verifiable by: ! grep -q 'warnAndReturnEmpty' src/adapters/podcast.ts ) @implemented

# rendering
- The Dashboard is fully server-rendered HTML with no client-side JavaScript; it works in any browser, including on mobile, and updates require a page reload or explicit refresh

# domain
- a Dashboard is the self-hosted web interface that displays aggregated, deduplicated, and optionally LLM-processed content from many sources in a single customizable view
- a Source is a content provider (Hacker News, Reddit, arXiv, RSS feeds, GitHub releases, podcasts, etc.) that a user configures to pull Items into the Dashboard
- an Item is a single piece of content (story, paper, video, release note, etc.) shown in the Dashboard, with title, link, publication time, and optional summary or body
- a Panel is a section of the Dashboard that shows a curated list of Items from one or more Sources after the user's configured Transforms have been applied
- a Transform is a processing step (deduplicate, keyword filter/exclude, keep latest N, LLM summarize/rank/filter, time decay scoring, etc.) that the user declares in their Config to control which Items appear and in what order
- a Config is the single YAML file in which the user declares Sources with their refresh schedules, the sequence of Transforms to apply, the recursive flexbox Layout of Panels, and optional LLM provider settings
- a Preset is a ready-to-use Config file (tech-news, ml-ai, academic-papers, product-launches, etc.) that can be selected with --preset or -P so a user can get a working Dashboard instantly without writing YAML
- a Refresh updates the Items for a Panel (or all Panels) by re-fetching from the underlying Sources, re-applying Transforms, and redrawing the Dashboard; users can trigger it manually via a button or it happens on the schedule defined per Source
- LLM-powered Transforms (summarize, filter, rank by interests) are optional; when no LLM is configured or the provider is unreachable, the Dashboard still works normally using only the non-LLM Transforms
- the entire system runs as a single Docker container (or local Bun process) serving server-rendered HTML with no client-side JavaScript; the Dashboard is responsive and works on phones, tablets, and desktops

# content

## dedup
- Items from different Sources that point to the same story are automatically deduplicated so a user does not see the same link multiple times in one Panel

## filtering
- Users can add keyword filters or excludes in their Config so that, for example, hiring posts or off-topic content never appear in the Dashboard

# usage

## refresh
- Clicking the refresh button on a Panel immediately fetches the latest Items from its Sources and updates the view without restarting the server

## startup
- Running 'pace' or 'pace serve' (or the Docker image) starts a web server on port 7453 by default and begins populating the Dashboard from the configured Sources within seconds

## onboarding
- The Dashboard works with zero configuration using the built-in example (or any Preset) and requires no database setup beyond the automatically created data/ directory
- A user can go from zero to a useful personalized tech/news/research Dashboard in under a minute by running the Docker image with --preset tech-news or ml-ai

# llm

## user-experience
- When an LLM is configured, Items can show AI-written summaries and be sorted according to the user's stated interests; without an LLM the same Transforms and layout still work

# cli

## usage
- The CLI accepts --config to point at a custom YAML file and --port to change the listening port; --help shows all options

# reliability
- If a Source is temporarily unreachable, the Dashboard continues to show the last successfully fetched Items for that Source instead of going blank or crashing

# code-quality
- transforms.ts ContentItemRow handling uses only the current panel_id field name (post DB rename from adapter_name column); the two obsolete .adapter_name references (in contentItemToRow and cluster signal extraction) have been removed so rows always conform to the ContentItemRow interface and source fallback uses panel_id when applicable (verifiable by: ! grep -q "adapter_name" src/transforms.ts ) @implemented
- config.ts validateAdapterConfig reuses validateOptionalNonEmptyString for the optional adapter.name field (no inline duplication of the typeof+trim non-empty check logic that the helper already provides and which is used for similar optional string fields like half_life/criteria/prompt); verifiable by: grep -q "validateOptionalNonEmptyString(adapter.name" src/config.ts @implemented
- core modules cli.ts/config.ts/index.ts/scheduler.ts no longer import shared helpers (errorMessage, parsePort, isValidPort, getAdapterName) from ./adapters/types.ts violating layer boundaries (Convention Blindness); instead they import from canonical src/utils.ts, and src/adapters/types.ts reexports only for its internal/adapter compat (verifiable by: grep -q 'from ["\./]utils' src/cli.ts && grep -q 'from ["\./]utils' src/config.ts && grep -q 'from ["\./]utils' src/index.ts && grep -q 'from ["\./]utils' src/scheduler.ts && ! grep -E 'from ["\./]*adapters/types' src/{cli,config,index,scheduler}.ts | grep -E '(errorMessage|parsePort|isValidPort|getAdapterName)' && grep -q 'from "../utils"' src/adapters/types.ts ) @implemented
- scheduler.ts pruneOldItems uses errorMessage(err) in console.warn (consistent with project errorMessage convention and the executeWithRunningGuard catch in same file) instead of logging raw err, while keeping exact warn+continue semantics with no rethrow (verifiable by: grep -q "scheduler: prune error:" src/scheduler.ts && ! grep -q "prune error:, err" src/scheduler.ts && grep -q "errorMessage(err)" src/scheduler.ts ) @implemented
- src/db.ts getDb() and closeDb() no longer contain bare 'catch {}' silent swallows on db.close(); instead they use errorMessage(err) in a console.warn (for debuggability and convention consistency with scheduler/b5h and db error prefixes) while still swallowing to preserve original shutdown/switch behavior (verifiable by: grep -q 'db: close error:' src/db.ts && grep -q 'errorMessage(err)' src/db.ts && ! grep -E 'catch\s*\{\s*\}' src/db.ts ) @implemented
- src/index.ts contains no over-engineered isAllAdapter helper function (nor its formal JSDoc claiming "Single source of truth for the special \"all\" adapter sentinel"); the predicate is inlined at its three call sites using the direct `=== "all"` check for improved readability with no behavior change (verifiable by: ! grep -q "isAllAdapter" src/index.ts && ! grep -q "Single source of truth for the special" src/index.ts ) @implemented
- src/layout.tsx contains no over-verbose defaultFlex tiny wrapper helper function (nor its call from flexStyle); default flex logic (f ?? 1) is inlined directly inside flexStyle; flexStyle has no restating JSDoc comment block claiming to be a 'Shared helper to avoid repeating' the flex pattern (verifiable by: ! grep -q 'function defaultFlex' src/layout.tsx && ! grep -q 'Shared helper to avoid repeating' src/layout.tsx && grep -q 'flex:${f ?? 1}' src/layout.tsx ) @implemented
- src/cli.ts contains no verbosity-inflating restating comments for the projectRoot chdir bootstrap (the 3-line 'Ensure we always run...' block) or the unknown-options rejection (the 2-line 'Reject unknown options...' block); both have been removed so code stands alone without duplication of its own intent (verifiable by: ! grep -q 'Ensure we always run from the project root' src/cli.ts && ! grep -q 'Reject unknown options' src/cli.ts ) @implemented
